From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leo Lee <leolee@microsoft.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 23:21:09 -0700
Subject: Avoid re-entrant slot assignment recalc

SlotAssignment::RecalcAssignment() could be re-entered for the same
shadow root while it was still walking its slot list, because
HTMLSlotElement::DidRecalcAssignedNodes() can run script. Bail out of
the re-entrant call instead. needs_assignment_recalc_ stays set, so the
pending work is picked up by the next lifecycle update.

The script came from HTMLInputElement::DidChangeIsInCanvasSubtree(),
which cleared the suggested value even when there was none. That
rebuilds date fields and moves focus. Skip the clear when there is
nothing to hide. An active autofill preview can still reach this path,
so the guard stays until crbug.com/574469802 moves that work out of
recalc.

Script run from that loop can also rebuild the slot list without
re-entering recalc, so the loop now iterates a copy and skips slots
that have left the shadow root. Earlier fixes in this area use the same
kind of defensive copy.

Fixed: 573335176
Change-Id: Icd4a8f6405d65292a9527002773542ccbc911d56
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8592884
Commit-Queue: Leo Lee <leolee@microsoft.com>
Reviewed-by: Dan Clark <daniec@microsoft.com>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1724473}

